    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45807" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub-dĭālis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subdīvālis</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 19, 11, 4</span></i>), e,
			adj.
		dius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that is in the open air</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inambulationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 1, 3, § 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">petrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					34, 12, 29, § 117</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subdĭālĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>open galleries</i> or <i>terraces;</i> a transl.
			of the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαίθρια, ὕπαιθρα</span>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				36, 25, 62, § 186</span></i>.—Also in
				sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subdival domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Jud. 11</span></i>
			.</div>
